<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="FB_FemtoAmplifier" Id="{d17b9fcd-ee8c-4366-b2d6-41b5b869217b}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    FB_FemtoAmplifier - Femto DLPCA-200 current amplifier, remote controlled

    Sets gain, low-noise/high-speed mode and AC/DC coupling of a DLPCA-200
    through its digital control inputs, reads back its overload output,
    reports a settling state after every change, and converts the voltage
    measured by an analog input block into the amplifier's input current.

    Gain code on pins 12..10: GainExponent - 3 in low-noise mode,
    GainExponent - 5 in high-speed mode. Code 7 is never output.

    After a PLC start the gain is 10^3 V/A, low noise, DC coupling, the
    settling time 150 ms, and the state SETTLING. Cfg is not retained.

    I/O (link in the I/O configuration), DLPCA-200 control port (Sub-D 25):
        GainBit0    AT %Q*  BOOL  pin 10, gain LSB         5 V output, e.g. EL2124
        GainBit1    AT %Q*  BOOL  pin 11, gain
        GainBit2    AT %Q*  BOOL  pin 12, gain MSB
        DcCoupling  AT %Q*  BOOL  pin 13, TRUE = DC        optional
        LowNoise    AT %Q*  BOOL  pin 14, TRUE = low noise
        Overload    AT %I*  BOOL  pin 5, TRUE = overload   5 V input, e.g. EL1124
    Pin 9 is the ground of the control inputs (pins 10..14), pin 3 the
    ground of the overload output. The control inputs take 2.3..12 V as HIGH.
    The remote bits are ORed with the local switches: set them to "Remote",
    "AC" and "H" (high speed). If DcCoupling is not linked, the local AC/DC
    switch decides the coupling. Bandwidth (FBW/10 Hz) and bias are local
    only.

    Use from ST, every cycle, the analog input block first:
        Ai1();                          // measures the amplifier output
        Femto1(Input := Ai1);           // FB_AnalogInput16 or 32
        Acq.Channel[1].Input := Femto1.Status.CurrentA;
    In the reverse order, the current lags by one cycle and the filter
    restart at the end of settling comes one cycle late.

    Input (ST only):
        Input   REFERENCE TO FB_AnalogInputBase
                analog input block that measures the amplifier's output
                voltage. Without it the block reports an error and the
                currents read 0; the control outputs work as usual.

    Cfg (written by the client, all live):
        GainExponent    INT   gain 10^GainExponent V/A: 3..9 with LowNoise
                              TRUE, 5..11 with LowNoise FALSE; default 3.
                              GainExponent and LowNoise are validated as a
                              pair. An invalid pair is reported as an error
                              while present, and the last valid pair stays in
                              use. When switching mode, the error between two
                              writes is harmless.
        LowNoise        BOOL  TRUE = low-noise mode, FALSE = high-speed mode;
                              default TRUE
        DcCoupling      BOOL  TRUE = DC, FALSE = AC coupling; default TRUE
        SettlingTimeMs  REAL  ms, >= 0, rounded to whole cycles; default 150.
                              A negative value is reported as an error while
                              present, and the last valid value stays. A
                              change applies from the next settling period on;
                              with 0 the state is READY in the cycle of the
                              change.

    Status (read only):
        State             INT         0 READY, 1 SETTLING (see E_FemtoState).
                                      SETTLING for the settling time after
                                      every change of gain, mode or coupling
                                      in use and after a PLC start; a further
                                      change restarts the settling time.
        StateText         STRING(20)  'READY' or 'SETTLING'
        Error             BOOL        TRUE while Input is not assigned, the
                                      gain pair is invalid, or SettlingTimeMs
                                      is negative. An overload is no error.
        ErrorText         STRING(80)  the first of these that applies:
                                      'Input not assigned (analog input block
                                      of the amplifier output)',
                                      e.g. 'GainExponent 12 outside 5..11
                                      (high speed)',
                                      'SettlingTimeMs must be >= 0'
        Settling          BOOL        TRUE while SETTLING
        GainExponent      INT         gain exponent in use
        LowNoise          BOOL        mode in use, TRUE = low noise
        DcCoupling        BOOL        coupling in use, TRUE = DC
        GainVPerA         REAL        V/A; gain in use, 10^GainExponent
        SettlingTimeMs    REAL        ms; effective settling time, used from
                                      the next settling period on
        Overload          BOOL        overload output of the amplifier
        CurrentA          REAL        A; Input.Status.Value / GainVPerA, with
                                      the gain in use in the same cycle. The
                                      amplifier does not invert.
        CurrentFilteredA  REAL        A; while READY
                                      Input.Status.ValueFiltered / GainVPerA.
                                      While SETTLING and in the cycle settling
                                      ends, equal to CurrentA. When settling
                                      ends, the block restarts the input's
                                      moving average (Input.RestartFilter()),
                                      so values taken at different gains are
                                      never averaged together.
*)
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_FemtoAmplifier
VAR_INPUT
    Cfg : ST_FemtoCfg;
    Input : REFERENCE TO FB_AnalogInputBase;
    Overload AT %I* : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    Status : ST_FemtoStatus;
    GainBit0 AT %Q* : BOOL;
    GainBit1 AT %Q* : BOOL;
    GainBit2 AT %Q* : BOOL;
    LowNoise AT %Q* : BOOL;
    DcCoupling AT %Q* : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR
    State : E_FemtoState := E_FemtoState.SETTLING;
    // FALSE until the first call after a PLC start.
    Started : BOOL;

    // Settings in use: the last valid configuration.
    GainExponentInUse : INT := 3;
    LowNoiseInUse : BOOL := TRUE;
    DcCouplingInUse : BOOL := TRUE;
    SettlingTimeMs : REAL := 150.0;
    // Gain code on pins 12..10 and gain in V/A of the settings in use.
    GainCode : INT;
    GainVPerA : LREAL := 1.0E3;

    // Settling period: length taken at its start, and cycles elapsed.
    SettlingCycles : UDINT;
    ElapsedCycles : UDINT;
    // TRUE in the call in which settling ends.
    SettlingEnded : BOOL;

    // Condition errors, empty while the condition is absent.
    InputText : STRING(80);
    GainText : STRING(80);
    SettlingText : STRING(80);
END_VAR
VAR CONSTANT
    LOW_NOISE_MIN_EXPONENT : INT := 3;
    LOW_NOISE_MAX_EXPONENT : INT := 9;
    HIGH_SPEED_MIN_EXPONENT : INT := 5;
    HIGH_SPEED_MAX_EXPONENT : INT := 11;
    LOW_NOISE_RANGE_TEXT : STRING(40) := ' outside 3..9 (low noise)';
    HIGH_SPEED_RANGE_TEXT : STRING(40) := ' outside 5..11 (high speed)';
    INPUT_TEXT : STRING(80) := 'Input not assigned (analog input block of the amplifier output)';
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[
// 1. Live configuration. Every setting counts as changed in the first call.
UpdateSettling(Changed := ApplyConfiguration() OR NOT Started);
Started := TRUE;

// 2. Outputs
GainBit0 := GainCode.0;
GainBit1 := GainCode.1;
GainBit2 := GainCode.2;
LowNoise := LowNoiseInUse;
DcCoupling := DcCouplingInUse;

// 3. Input current, after settling so that the filter restart lands in the
//    cycle settling ends
UpdateCurrent();

// 4. Status
UpdateStatus();
]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
    <Method Name="ApplyConfiguration" Id="{4ff8a9e5-8054-49d4-bab4-da1a8d899fcb}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    Validates the live Cfg and applies the valid parts to the settings in
    use. Returns TRUE if gain, mode or coupling in use changed.
*)
METHOD PRIVATE ApplyConfiguration : BOOL
VAR
    MinExponent : INT;
    MaxExponent : INT;
    RangeText : STRING(40);
    Power : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
ApplyConfiguration := FALSE;

// Gain and mode, validated as a pair
IF Cfg.LowNoise THEN
    MinExponent := LOW_NOISE_MIN_EXPONENT;
    MaxExponent := LOW_NOISE_MAX_EXPONENT;
    RangeText := LOW_NOISE_RANGE_TEXT;
ELSE
    MinExponent := HIGH_SPEED_MIN_EXPONENT;
    MaxExponent := HIGH_SPEED_MAX_EXPONENT;
    RangeText := HIGH_SPEED_RANGE_TEXT;
END_IF
IF Cfg.GainExponent >= MinExponent AND Cfg.GainExponent <= MaxExponent THEN
    IF Cfg.GainExponent <> GainExponentInUse OR Cfg.LowNoise <> LowNoiseInUse THEN
        ApplyConfiguration := TRUE;
    END_IF
    GainExponentInUse := Cfg.GainExponent;
    LowNoiseInUse := Cfg.LowNoise;
    GainCode := Cfg.GainExponent - MinExponent;
    GainText := '';
ELSE
    GainText := CONCAT(CONCAT('GainExponent ', INT_TO_STRING(Cfg.GainExponent)), RangeText);
END_IF

// Gain in V/A, exact in LREAL for all valid exponents
GainVPerA := 1.0;
FOR Power := 1 TO GainExponentInUse DO
    GainVPerA := GainVPerA * 10.0;
END_FOR

// Coupling, always valid
IF Cfg.DcCoupling <> DcCouplingInUse THEN
    ApplyConfiguration := TRUE;
END_IF
DcCouplingInUse := Cfg.DcCoupling;

// Settling time, used from the next settling period on
IF Cfg.SettlingTimeMs >= 0.0 THEN
    SettlingTimeMs := Cfg.SettlingTimeMs;
    SettlingText := '';
ELSE
    SettlingText := 'SettlingTimeMs must be >= 0';
END_IF
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="UpdateCurrent" Id="{b7c98860-9217-4674-9e1b-d2c725164b0f}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    Converts the input voltage into the input current with the gain in use,
    and restarts the input's moving average when settling ends.
*)
METHOD PRIVATE UpdateCurrent
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
IF NOT __ISVALIDREF(Input) THEN
    InputText := INPUT_TEXT;
    Status.CurrentA := 0.0;
    Status.CurrentFilteredA := 0.0;
    RETURN;
END_IF
InputText := '';

Status.CurrentA := LREAL_TO_REAL(REAL_TO_LREAL(Input.Status.Value) / GainVPerA);
IF State = E_FemtoState.READY AND NOT SettlingEnded THEN
    Status.CurrentFilteredA := LREAL_TO_REAL(REAL_TO_LREAL(Input.Status.ValueFiltered) / GainVPerA);
ELSE
    // The input's average may still contain values from before the change.
    Status.CurrentFilteredA := Status.CurrentA;
END_IF

IF SettlingEnded THEN
    Input.RestartFilter();
END_IF
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="UpdateSettling" Id="{0a0b7139-7a60-464d-a46a-e7edbc8c04c5}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    Starts a settling period on a change of the settings in use, with the
    settling time valid at that moment, and ends it after that time.
*)
METHOD PRIVATE UpdateSettling
VAR_INPUT
    Changed : BOOL;     // gain, mode or coupling in use changed in this call
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
SettlingEnded := FALSE;

IF Changed THEN
    SettlingCycles := F_MsToCycles(TimeMs := SettlingTimeMs);
    ElapsedCycles := 0;
    State := E_FemtoState.SETTLING;
END_IF

IF State = E_FemtoState.SETTLING THEN
    IF ElapsedCycles >= SettlingCycles THEN
        State := E_FemtoState.READY;
        SettlingEnded := TRUE;
    ELSE
        ElapsedCycles := ElapsedCycles + 1;
    END_IF
END_IF
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="UpdateStatus" Id="{a06864d9-56d5-44b2-97d0-68e148c95aa1}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
METHOD PRIVATE UpdateStatus
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
Status.State := TO_INT(State);
Status.StateText := TO_STRING(State);

IF InputText <> '' THEN
    Status.Error := TRUE;
    Status.ErrorText := InputText;
ELSIF GainText <> '' THEN
    Status.Error := TRUE;
    Status.ErrorText := GainText;
ELSIF SettlingText <> '' THEN
    Status.Error := TRUE;
    Status.ErrorText := SettlingText;
ELSE
    Status.Error := FALSE;
    Status.ErrorText := '';
END_IF

Status.Settling := State = E_FemtoState.SETTLING;
Status.GainExponent := GainExponentInUse;
Status.LowNoise := LowNoiseInUse;
Status.DcCoupling := DcCouplingInUse;
Status.GainVPerA := LREAL_TO_REAL(GainVPerA);
Status.SettlingTimeMs := F_CyclesToMs(Cycles := F_MsToCycles(TimeMs := SettlingTimeMs));
Status.Overload := Overload;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>